Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(graph):=20proxy=20clips=20play=20through=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?WaveNodeRealTime=20=E2=80=94=20no=20more=202-sample=20lag?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A clip whose canUseProxy() is true (every compressed source — FLAC, MP3, OGG — and every
reversed clip) was built by createNodeForAudioClip as the legacy WaveNode / SpeedRampWaveNode.
Its processSection feeds a juce::LagrangeInterpolator from the file start without compensating
the interpolator's base latency, so the file sounded 2 SOURCE samples late at every rate pair,
and always in Lagrange whatever the clip's ResamplingQuality. The proxy branch now builds a
WaveNodeRealTime on the proxy file, like every other clip (speed-fade description kept, time
stretch disabled: the proxy is already rendered).

The other users of the legacy nodes move too, so none is left outside the engine's own tests:
the frozen-track and group-freeze nodes (EditNodeBuilder), createWaveNodeForFile and the
tape start/stop effect (ClipEffects), and the comp render (CompManager).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
